IMPORT prelude

-- Small Motorised Vehicles (Safety) Act 2020 (Singapore) -- what counts as a personal mobility device, power-assisted
-- bicycle or small motorised vehicle (s 2), importing without approval (s 5), keeping an unsafe device and who is presumed
-- to keep it (ss 8A, 8B), entry into homes (s 10(2)), seizure without warrant and notice of it (s 11), refusing to answer
-- (s 12(6)), false information (s 13), the composition cap (s 14), forfeiture by the Authority (s 15(2), (3)) and when
-- refusing an officer is not obstruction (s 19).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021), informal consolidation "version in force
-- from 1/6/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SMVSA2020.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 5 of
-- 2026 wef 01/06/2026, which added Part 2A (keeping unsafe devices).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: e-scooters and power-assisted bicycles are ridden, bought and kept
-- in flats across Singapore, and since 1 June 2026 merely keeping one that fails the safety requirements can be an
-- offence. SCOPED to what an owner, rider or occupier meets. Not encoded: s 8 (breach of the purpose of an import
-- approval), s 7 (cancellation of import approvals and the appeal), the detail of the s 10 entry powers, administration
-- (ss 16-18), secrecy (s 20), corporate and partnership liability (ss 22, 23), service of documents (s 25), and the
-- regulations (the safety requirements themselves, import approval conditions, prescribed circumstances and the list of
-- compoundable offences were not retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Small Motorised Vehicles (Safety) Act 2020 -- devices`

§§ `2 -- personal mobility devices, power-assisted bicycles, small motorised vehicles`

-- s 2(1): "personal mobility device" means (a) a wheeled vehicle that "(i) is built to transport people only (with or without
-- carry-on baggage); (ii) is suitable for use on land other than a railway; and (iii) is propelled by an electric motor
-- attached to the vehicle or by human power and such a motor"; (b) a partly assembled and substantially complete vehicle;
-- or (c) "an unassembled or a completely knocked-down vehicle" -- "but does not include a power-assisted bicycle, trolley,
-- inline skates or a wheeled toy".
-- "power-assisted bicycle" means (a) a bicycle that "(i) is equipped with an electric motor; and (ii) may be propelled by
-- human power or by the electric motor ... or by both", with the same (b) and (c).
-- "small motorised vehicle" means (a) a PMD; (b) a PAB; or (c) a prescribed type of motorised land vehicle.
-- s 1(2): paragraph (c) of both definitions (the unassembled kit) comes into operation "on a date that the Minister appoints
-- by notification in the Gazette". The deposit does not say whether that date has been appointed, so it is an input here.
--
-- A kick scooter with no motor is not a PMD: the motor is part of the definition.
DECLARE Assembly IS ONE OF
    `fully assembled`
    `partly assembled and substantially complete`
    `unassembled or completely knocked down`

DECLARE Vehicle HAS
    `is wheeled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is built to transport people only` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is suitable for land other than a railway` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an electric motor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a bicycle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a trolley, inline skates or a wheeled toy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a prescribed type of motorised land vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assembly` IS AN Assembly

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `paragraph (c) is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assembly state is covered` IF
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`'s `assembly`
    WHEN `fully assembled` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `partly assembled and substantially complete` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `unassembled or completely knocked down` THEN `paragraph (c) is in operation`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `paragraph (c) is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is a power-assisted bicycle` IF
        `the vehicle`'s `is a bicycle`
    AND `the vehicle`'s `has an electric motor`
    AND `the assembly state is covered` `the vehicle` `paragraph (c) is in operation`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `paragraph (c) is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is a personal mobility device` IF
        `the vehicle`'s `is wheeled`
    AND `the vehicle`'s `is built to transport people only`
    AND `the vehicle`'s `is suitable for land other than a railway`
    AND `the vehicle`'s `has an electric motor`
    AND (NOT `the vehicle is a power-assisted bicycle` `the vehicle` `paragraph (c) is in operation`)
    AND (NOT `the vehicle`'s `is a trolley, inline skates or a wheeled toy`)
    AND `the assembly state is covered` `the vehicle` `paragraph (c) is in operation`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `paragraph (c) is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is a small motorised vehicle` IF
        `the vehicle is a personal mobility device` `the vehicle` `paragraph (c) is in operation`
    OR  `the vehicle is a power-assisted bicycle` `the vehicle` `paragraph (c) is in operation`
    OR  `the vehicle`'s `is a prescribed type of motorised land vehicle`

§§ `5 -- importing without approval`

-- s 5(1): an offence if the person imports a small motorised vehicle and "at the time of import, the person is not permitted
-- to import" it. (2): permitted if, at the time of import, (a) the person "is granted an import approval", it is in force
-- and the vehicle is specified or described in it; (b) the person "is authorised, in writing, by the person who is granted
-- an import approval", it is in force and the vehicle is specified in it; or (c) "a circumstance prescribed in the
-- regulations applies".
GIVEN `holds an import approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `is authorised in writing by a holder` IS A BOOLEAN, `the approval is in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `the vehicle is specified in the approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `a prescribed circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is permitted to import` IF
        (   (`holds an import approval` OR `is authorised in writing by a holder`)
        AND `the approval is in force`
        AND `the vehicle is specified in the approval`
        )
    OR  `a prescribed circumstance applies`

GIVEN `imports a small motorised vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `is permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `importing is an offence` IF
    `imports a small motorised vehicle` AND (NOT `is permitted`)

-- ss 5(4), 8A(3): "repeat offender" -- convicted of the current offence and convicted of the same offence "on at least one
-- other earlier occasion within the period of 5 years immediately before" the current conviction. Counting a conviction
-- exactly 5 years earlier as within the period is an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `has an earlier conviction for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `years between the convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a repeat offender` IF
    `has an earlier conviction for the same offence` AND `years between the convictions` AT MOST 5

-- s 5(3): (a) an individual -- "$5,000 or ... 6 months or ... both"; repeat offender "$10,000 or ... 12 months"; (b) any other
-- case -- $10,000; repeat offender $20,000. No imprisonment for a non-individual (0 here).
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for unapproved import` IS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `repeat` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000
    ELSE IF `repeat` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum months for unapproved import` IS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `repeat` THEN 12 ELSE 6
    ELSE 0

§§ `8A, 8B -- keeping an unsafe device`

-- s 2(1): "unsafe device" means "a small motorised vehicle that does not comply with the safety requirements prescribed for
-- that class or description". s 8A(1): an offence if the person, "without reasonable excuse, keeps an unsafe device at any
-- place knowing that, or reckless as to whether, the device is an unsafe device".
GIVEN `keeps an unsafe device` IS A BOOLEAN, `knows or is reckless that it is unsafe` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeping is an offence` IF
    `keeps an unsafe device` AND `knows or is reckless that it is unsafe` AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 8A(2): an individual -- $2,000 or 3 months; repeat $5,000 or 6 months. Any other case -- $4,000; repeat $10,000.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for keeping an unsafe device` IS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `repeat` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000
    ELSE IF `repeat` THEN 10000 ELSE 4000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum months for keeping an unsafe device` IS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `repeat` THEN 6 ELSE 3
    ELSE 0

-- s 8B(1): "(a) if there is a registered owner of the unsafe device -- the registered owner is presumed, unless the contrary is
-- proved, to be keeping" it; "(b) if paragraph (a) does not apply and the unsafe device is in the immediate possession of a
-- person -- the person"; "(c) if paragraphs (a) and (b) do not apply and the unsafe device is found within any premises
-- (other than any excluded premises) -- the occupier". (2): "excluded premises" are common property under the Town Councils
-- Act 1988, a public place under the Shared Mobility Enterprises (Control and Licensing) Act 2020, or prescribed premises.
--
-- The presumption runs to the registered owner first, even when someone else is holding the device.
DECLARE PresumedKeeper IS ONE OF
    `the registered owner`
    `the person in immediate possession`
    `the occupier of the premises`
    `no one is presumed`

GIVEN `there is a registered owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `someone has immediate possession` IS A BOOLEAN, `found within premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the premises are excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PresumedKeeper
DECIDE `who is presumed to keep the device` IS
    IF `there is a registered owner`
    THEN `the registered owner`
    ELSE IF `someone has immediate possession`
         THEN `the person in immediate possession`
         ELSE IF `found within premises` AND (NOT `the premises are excluded`)
              THEN `the occupier of the premises`
              ELSE `no one is presumed`

§§ `10(2) -- entering a home`

-- s 10(2)(a): an authorised officer is not authorised "to enter and search any relevant premises that is a place of
-- accommodation or residence, except (i) with the consent of the occupier; or (ii) under a warrant of a Magistrate's Court or
-- District Court". s 10(8): "relevant premises" include premises an officer believes on reasonable grounds are used for or
-- in connection with "the keeping of an unsafe device" (para (aa), added by Act 5 of 2026).
GIVEN `the premises are relevant premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the premises are a residence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is a court warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may enter and search` IF
        `the premises are relevant premises`
    AND (   (NOT `the premises are a residence`)
        OR  `the occupier consents`
        OR  `there is a court warrant`
        )

§§ `11 -- seizure without warrant`

-- s 11(1): where an authorised officer "has reason to believe" a small motorised vehicle or component is one "in connection
-- with which an offence under section 5, 8 or 8A has been or is being committed", the officer may, WITHOUT WARRANT, seize it
-- or require the owner or person in charge to surrender it at a holding yard. (2): whether or not the owner is present.
-- (3): notice of the seizure and grounds to the owner (if known) "except that the notice is not required to be given where
-- the seizure is made in the presence of the owner or the owner's agent". (4): refusing or neglecting to surrender without
-- reasonable excuse -- $1,000 or 3 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unapproved import`
    `breach of the purpose of an import approval`
    `keeping an unsafe device`
    `providing false information`
    `obstructing an officer`

GIVEN `the suspected offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle may be seized without warrant` IF
    CONSIDER `the suspected offence`
    WHEN `unapproved import` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `breach of the purpose of an import approval` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `keeping an unsafe device` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the owner is known` IS A BOOLEAN, `seized in the presence of the owner or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice of seizure must be given` IF
    `the owner is known` AND (NOT `seized in the presence of the owner or agent`)

§§ `12(6), 13 -- answering questions and false information`

-- s 12(1)(b): an offence to fail, "without reasonable excuse", to do anything required by an officer under s 10(1); (3) $5,000
-- or 6 months. (6): "it is a reasonable excuse for a person to refuse or fail to provide any information, produce any document
-- or answer any question if doing so might tend to incriminate that person".
GIVEN `failed to comply with a requirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `answering might incriminate them` IS A BOOLEAN, `has another reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to comply is an offence` IF
        `failed to comply with a requirement`
    AND (NOT `answering might incriminate them`)
    AND (NOT `has another reasonable excuse`)

-- s 13(1): providing a document, statement or information to the Authority or an officer that is false or misleading (or
-- misleadingly omits something), where the person "knows, or ought reasonably to know", in connection with an import approval
-- application or a question or request under the Act -- $5,000 or 12 months. (2): not if not false or misleading "in a
-- material particular".
GIVEN `the information is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought reasonably to know` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is material` IS A BOOLEAN, `given for an application or an official question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `giving the information is an offence` IF
        `the information is false or misleading`
    AND `knew or ought reasonably to know`
    AND `it is material`
    AND `given for an application or an official question`

§§ `14 -- composition`

-- s 14(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded. (2): by collecting "a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of ... (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000". (3): on
-- payment, no further proceedings.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the lower of` IS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most a composition may collect` IS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` / 2) 5000

§§ `15(2), (3) -- forfeiture by the Authority`

-- s 15(1): things seized or surrendered "are liable to forfeiture by a court". (2): the AUTHORITY may order forfeiture if
-- satisfied that "(a) the vehicle is a non-compliant personal mobility device, non-compliant power-assisted bicycle,
-- non-compliant mobility vehicle or unsafe device ...; (b) an offence under this Act has been committed and the vehicle was ...
-- the subject matter, or was ... used in the commission, of the offence; (c) at the end of 30 days after the date of the
-- seizure or surrender, no claim ... is earlier made" by a person other than the person it was seized from or required to
-- surrender it (or their agent); "and (d) a person is convicted of the offence, or ... has that offence compounded".
-- (3): "Despite subsection (2), the Authority may at once order the forfeiture" of a non-compliant or unsafe vehicle that it
-- considers "would be dangerous to retain", or whose detention "materially increases the likelihood of an outbreak of fire at
-- the holding yard".
--
-- Read as written, (a) to (d) are cumulative. The owner's own claim does not block forfeiture; only a third party's does.
GIVEN `the vehicle is non-compliant or unsafe` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was the subject of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `a third party has claimed it` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted or compounded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may order forfeiture` IF
        `the vehicle is non-compliant or unsafe`
    AND `it was the subject of an offence`
    AND `days since seizure` AT LEAST 30
    AND (NOT `a third party has claimed it`)
    AND `convicted or compounded`

GIVEN `the vehicle is non-compliant or unsafe` IS A BOOLEAN, `dangerous to retain` IS A BOOLEAN, `detention raises fire risk at the yard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may forfeit at once` IF
        `the vehicle is non-compliant or unsafe`
    AND (`dangerous to retain` OR `detention raises fire risk at the yard`)

§§ `19 -- obstruction`

-- s 19(1): refusing access to, or obstructing, hindering or delaying an authorised officer -- $5,000 or 6 months. (2): "it is
-- not an offence ... to refuse to comply with any request, demand or order made or given by an authorised officer who (a)
-- fails to declare his or her office; AND (b) refuses to produce his or her identification card on demand".
--
-- Both failures are needed. An officer who declares the office but will not show a card can still be obeyed on pain of
-- prosecution, as read here.
GIVEN `refused the officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer declared the office` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer produced the card on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the officer is an offence` IF
        `refused the officer`
    AND (`the officer declared the office` OR `the officer produced the card on demand`)
